{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And he said to the wicked one: Why do you strike your fellow?</b> Rashi explained: even though he had not struck him, by the raising of a hand he is called wicked. 'Your fellow' — a wicked man like yourself. But this is difficult: who told Moses that this one was wicked like him? And furthermore, where is it written that he sought to strike him, since it is not stated 'and he raised his hand to strike him'? And it appears to me that the language of striking applies also to speech, as it is written (Proverbs 12:18) ״יֵשׁ בּוֹטֶה כְּמַדְקְרוֹת חָרֶב״, and it is written (Deuteronomy 27:24) ״אָרוּר מַכֵּה רֵעֵהוּ בַּסָּתֶר״, for one who casts a blemish upon his fellow — there is no greater blow than this. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said (Kiddushin 40a): 'Whoever disqualifies, disqualifies with his own blemish.' Now Moses saw two Hebrew men quarreling with reviling and blasphemy, and if so, both were wicked, for the trait of the righteous is to be among the insulted and not to insult, to hear the voice of a reviler and not answer back. And he called him 'your fellow' — a wicked man exactly like yourself, for by that same blemish with which you disqualify him and strike him with the lash of your tongue, that same blemish is surely found also in you, for 'whoever disqualifies, disqualifies with his own blemish.' Therefore he said, 'Why do you strike your fellow?' — for he is your fellow in this blemish." "And the proof of this, that there was no striking by hand here but rather by mouth, is from what he said: 'Do you mean to kill me?' — do you intend to kill me with the words of your mouth, to repay me measure for measure? Have I not yet actually killed anyone, that you should consider killing me — for such is your way, to increase the punishment beyond the sin: the Egyptian was also striking a Hebrew man, and you killed him; so too you plan to do to me."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:17:59.644155909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}